      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The community first settled in the late 1800s, serving as a key stop for timber raftsmen moving logs down the Allegheny River to Pittsburgh.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.trawellino.com/destinations/united-states/pennsylvania_reservoir",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Reservoir sits on the south side of the valley of the Frankstown Branch Juniata River, a tributary of the Juniata.",
